# 4. REAL DOCUMENT INGESTION SYSTEM

This is one of the most important parts of the project.

Do not rely on manually written example answers.

Build an actual document ingestion pipeline.

### Supported document types

- PDF.
- DOCX.
- TXT.
- HTML webpages.
- CSV, where appropriate.
- Officially published document links.

### Ingestion workflow

1. Admin enters an official source URL or uploads an official document.
2. Backend validates the URL and file type.
3. System downloads or reads the document.
4. Extract text from the document.
5. For PDFs, extract text and page information.
6. Detect scanned PDFs and use OCR when necessary.
7. Clean extracted text without removing important legal language.
8. Split content into meaningful chunks.
9. Preserve headings, section numbers, page numbers, document title, and source URL.
10. Generate embeddings.
11. Store the original document metadata and extracted content.
12. Save embeddings in the vector database.
13. Make the document available for retrieval.
14. Record ingestion status, timestamps, and errors.

### Metadata required for every document

Store:

- Document ID.
- Document title.
- Issuing authority.
- Source URL.
- Document type.
- Document number, if available.
- Publication date, if available.
- Effective date, if available.
- Last updated date, if available.
- Retrieval date.
- Document version.
- Language.
- Page count.
- Verification status.
- Superseded status.
- Previous version reference.
- File checksum/hash.
- Ingestion status.

Never assume the download date is the publication date.

If a publication or effective date is unavailable, display "Date not stated in source."

### Document update management

Implement:

- Duplicate document detection.
- Content hash comparison.
- Version history.
- Updated-document detection.
- Superseded-document marking.
- Re-indexing when a document changes.
- Admin review before publishing high-impact updates.

Do not automatically delete older documents. Retain historical versions and identify them clearly.

If two official sources conflict, show the conflict and ask for human review rather than silently choosing one.

